  "confidence": 0.86,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": [
        "U1",
        "D3",
        "J8",
        "R2",
        "R5",
        "C7",
        "TP4",
        "D6"
      ],
      "pins": [
        "U1.8",
        "U1.31",
        "D3.1",
        "D3.3",
        "J8.3"
      ],
      "nets": [
        "Net-(D3-A)",
        "FAN_1_TACH"
      ],
      "observed": "The fan tachometer signal for J8 is connected through D3 to Net-(D3-A), and that same net contains both ESP32-C3 pin 8 (EN/CHIP_PU) and pin 31 (GPIO21/U0TXD). In other words, the FAN_1_TACH line is coupled to the MCU enable/reset net and to another MCU pin.",
      "expected": "EN/CHIP_PU should be a reset/enable input with its pull-up and decoupling network only, not tied to a fan tachometer input or to GPIO21/U0TXD. Fan tach inputs should be independent GPIO/input signals so that firmware can monitor them and raise a fault, as described in the specification.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"15\") (name \"Net-(D3-A)\") ... (node (ref \"D3\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"A\") ... (node (ref \"U1\") (pin \"31\") (pinfunction \"GPIO21/U0TXD\") ... (node (ref \"U1\") (pin \"8\") (pinfunction \"EN/CHIP_PU\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"12\") (name \"FAN_1_TACH\") ... (node (ref \"D3\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"K\") ... (node (ref \"J8\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"Pin_3\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "Monitors **2 fan tachometers** (`NUM_FANS = 2`) with TVS-diode-protected inputs, and raises a run fault if a fan stalls."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "A low state on the FAN_1_TACH line can pull EN/CHIP_PU low through D3. Since standard fan tach outputs are open-collector/low pulses, a running fan could pulse the MCU enable pin, and a stalled fan could hold the MCU in reset or repeatedly reset it. This would prevent normal firmware operation and the intended software fan-fault reporting.",
      "confidence": 0.86
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows a fan tachometer input coupled into the ESP32-C3 EN/CHIP_PU net, which is not consistent with the intended fan-monitoring design and would likely cause MCU resets or lockout. No other anomaly is needed to explain a behavior deviation."
}

